  "notes": [
    "Game Boy side (B) of the 74LVC1T45s runs at VBUS (5 V): real 5 V levels, Ioff when unpowered (safe in any power order).",
    "PCB pins (short routes from the RP2350's bottom-left corner): GP12 SCK, GP13 data from GB (GB SOUT), GP14 data to GB (GB SIN), GP11 = SCK direction (left-side pin, routed above the fan). GP15 stays free: a core +3V3 trace under pad 20 blocks its way down. The breadboard uses GP0/1/2; the firmware selects the pins per board.",
    "Cable pad order puts ground between SCK and the data lines (crosstalk seen on the breadboard, LOGBOOK 2026-10-15).",
    "No SWD pads: the RP2350 is flashed over USB (BOOTSEL). SWD stays on the chip (RP2350 pins 24/25) if ever needed."
  ],
